Screen Translator — Terms of Use

1. The app is free for personal use at this stage.
2. All rights reserved. You may not sell, redistribute, re-upload, modify or decompile it without written permission. Share the official page link instead of the file.
3. Some features may become paid in later versions. What is free in your version keeps working in it.
4. Some features use online services (translation, natural voices, speech recognition), which receive the text or audio to be translated. Details, and how to keep everything on your device, are in Settings → Translation.
5. The app checks once a day for a new version and project announcements; you can turn this off in Settings → System.
6. The app is provided "as is", without any warranty. You are responsible for how you use it, and for respecting the rights of the content you translate or dub.
7. The app uses open-source components, each under its own license shipped with it.
